<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index fell three points to 1,280.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index fell three points to 1,280.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,280 today from 1,283 on Aug 4, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1362    12.369	  1374    12.475</p>
<p>   1a   1256  9513.000	  1259  9538.000</p>
<p>   2    1589    22.700	  1590    22.719</p>
<p>   2a   1508 12369.000	  1508 12369.000</p>
<p>   3    1381    12.744	  1383    12.763</p>
<p>   3a   1152  9094.000	  1151  9081.000</p>
